  "notes": "{心酔|しんすい} describes a state of being deeply captivated or devoted to something. The character {酔|すい} (intoxicated) suggests being 'drunk' with admiration.\n\nUSAGE:\n- Often used with に to indicate what one is captivated by\n- Can have a slightly negative nuance of being blindly devoted\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {傾倒|けいとう}: devotion, admiration\n- {夢中|むちゅう}: being absorbed in\n- {盲信|もうしん}: blind faith (more negative)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- Xに{心酔|しんすい}する: to be captivated by X\n- {心酔|しんすい}{者|しゃ}: an admirer, devotee",
